	(text "BMI270 ADDRESS STRAP - FIT ONE ONLY\n\n  R118 0R TO GND   FITTED -> 0x68 (DEFAULT)\n  R119 0R TO +3V3  DNP    -> 0x69 (REWORK)\n\nNEVER FIT BOTH: THAT SHORTS +3V3 TO GND.\n\n0x68 IS THE MOST COLLISION-PRONE ADDRESS ON A\nCOMMUNITY I2C BUS (MPU6050, ICM-20948, DS3231).\nTHIS PAIR IS THE NO-RESPIN ESCAPE UNDER D-049.\nIT REPLACES A HARD-WIRED SDO-TO-GND CONNECTION."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.0 130.0 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "fb050100-d100-4d10-9d10-0000000208")
	)
	(text "BMI270 STRAP AUDIT - BST-BMI270-DS000-08 REV 1.6\n\nPIN 1  SDO  -> GND VIA R118  = 0x68\nPIN 12 CSB  -> VDDIO         = I2C MODE.\n       BOSCH: HARD-WIRE THE CSB LINE TO VDDIO.\nPIN 2  ASDx -> VDDIO  |  SECONDARY I/F UNUSED.\nPIN 3  ASCx -> VDDIO  |  BOSCH: DO NOT CONNECT\n                      |  TO GND.\nPIN 9  INT2 -> DNC    = BOSCH INSTRUCTION\nPIN 10 OCSB -> DNC    = OIS UNUSED\nPIN 11 OSDO -> DNC    = OIS UNUSED\n\nC6 / C7 100nF: ONE AT PIN 5, ONE AT PIN 8.\nTHAT IS A PLACEMENT REQUIREMENT, NOT A NET.\n\nVDD 1.71-3.6 V, VDDIO 1.2-3.6 V, EITHER ORDER,\nNO SLEW CONSTRAINT. tPO 2 ms. FIFO 2048 BYTES.\nI2C 100 k / 400 k / 1 M (Fm+). Cin 5 pF.\n\nBMI270 HAS NO TAP OR DOUBLE-TAP FEATURE.\nRAISE-TO-WAKE = THE WRIST-WEAR-WAKEUP FEATURE.\n\nALWAYS POWERED FROM +3V3. NO LOAD SWITCH:\nACCEL LOW-POWER + FEATURES ~7-10 uA, AND A\nSWITCH WOULD DESTROY WAKE-ON-MOTION."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 215.0 40.0 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "fb050100-d100-4d10-9d10-0000000209")
	)
)
